{"type":"message","id":"02846cee","parentId":"b9585290","timestamp":"2026-03-21T02:26:42.423Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cf713884","toolName":"sessions_history","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:ceo:subagent:9026def8-ee54-4326-9c30-9f7869effd32\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"[Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\\n\\n[Subagent Task]: Create a comprehensive backend README.md file in the workspace-ceo/backend directory. The README should include:\\n\\n1. Setup instructions (venv, pip install, .env configuration)\\n2. All API endpoints with descriptions\\n3. Configuration options\\n4. How to run the server\\n\\nMake it production-ready and clear.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059682569\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\\nI need to explore the backend code to understand its structure before creating the README, so I'll list the files in the backend directory.\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\nI'll create a comprehensive backend README.md file. First, let me explore the backend directory to understand the project structure and API endpoints.\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_aa0316cf\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"ls -la /home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend/\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"vllm\",\n      \"model\": \"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059682574\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\\nLet me explore the backend directory structure to understand the project before creating the README.\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_0a603f69\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"find /home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend -type f -name \\\"*.py\\\" | head -20\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"vllm\",\n      \"model\": \"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059695195\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\\n\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_6f020192\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/app/main.py\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_9aabdeea\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/app/api/schemas.py\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_f290b8fc\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/.env.example\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_e59f0420\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/requirements.txt\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"vllm\",\n      \"model\": \"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059705126\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\\n\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\nNow let me check the scraper and cache modules to understand the full API structure:\\n\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_ca6f673f\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/app/scraper/livesport_scraper.py\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_34343153\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/app/cache/cache_manager.py\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"vllm\",\n      \"model\": \"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059708061\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\\nNow I have a complete understanding of the backend. Let me create a comprehensive README.md file with all the required sections.\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\nNow I have a complete understanding of the backend. Let me create a comprehensive README.md file:\\n\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_fef39dcc\",\n          \"name\": \"write\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"path\": \"backend/README.md\",\n            \"content\": \"# Live Football Dashboard API\\n\\nA FastAPI-based backend service that provides real-time football match data with caching and scheduling capabilities.\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- Real-time football match tracking\\n- In-memory caching with configurable TTL\\n- Background task scheduling for live data updates\\n- RESTful API endpoints\\n- Environment-based configuration\\n\\n## Setup Instructions\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\n\\n- Python 3.11+\\n- pip package manager\\n\\n### 1. Create Virtual Environment\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npython -m venv venv\\nsource venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\\\\Scripts\\\\activate\\n```\\n\\n### 2. Install Dependencies\\n\\n```bash\\npip install -r requirements.txt\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Configure Environment\\n\\nCopy the example environment file and configure your settings:\\n\\n```bash\\ncp .env.example .env\\n```\\n\\nEdit `.env` with your configuration:\\n\\n```env\\n# Livesport scraper base URL\\nLIVESPORT_URL=https://www.livesport.cz\\n\\n# Cache time-to-live in seconds (default: 60)\\nCACHE_TTL=60\\n\\n# Data update interval in seconds (default: 30)\\nUPDATE_INTERVAL=30\\n\\n# Enable debug mode (default: false)\\nDEBUG=false\\n```\\n\\n**Environment Variables:**\\n\\n| Variable | Description | Default | Required |\\n|----------|-------------|---------|----------|\\n| `LIVESPORT_URL` | Base URL for the livesport scraper | `https://www.livesport.cz` | No |\\n| `CACHE_TTL` | Cache time-to-live in seconds | `60` | No |\\n| `UPDATE_INTERVAL` | Background update interval in seconds | `30` | No |\\n| `DEBUG` | Enable debug mode (`true`/`false`) | `false` | No |\\n\\n## API Endpoints\\n\\n### Base URL\\n\\n```\\nhttp://localhost:8000\\n```\\n\\n### Endpoints\\n\\n#### `GET /`\\n\\n**Description:** API health check and root endpoint.\\n\\n**Response:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"message\\\": \\\"Live Football Dashboard API\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"running\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### `GET /api/live-matches`\\n\\n**Description:** Get all live football matches.\\n\\n**Response Code:** `200 OK`\\n\\n**Response Schema:** Array of `Match` objects.\\n\\n**Example Response:**\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"home_team\\\": \\\"FC Sparta Prague\\\",\\n    \\\"away_team\\\": \\\"FC Slavia Prague\\\",\\n    \\\"home_score\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"away_score\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"minute\\\": 67,\\n    \\\"league\\\": \\\"Czech Liga\\\",\\n    \\\"started_at\\\": \\\"2026-03-21T01:30:00\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"id\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"home_team\\\": \\\"Manchester United\\\",\\n    \\\"away_team\\\": \\\"Liverpool\\\",\\n    \\\"home_score\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"away_score\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"minute\\\": 89,\\n    \\\"league\\\": \\\"Premier League\\\",\\n    \\\"started_at\\\": \\\"2026-03-21T01:15:00\\\"\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\n**Match Object Schema:**\\n\\n| Field | Type | Description |\\n|-------|------|-------------|\\n| `id` | int | Unique match identifier |\\n| `home_team` | str | Home team name |\\n| `away_team` | str | Away team name |\\n| `home_score` | int | Home team current score |\\n| `away_score` | int | Away team current score |\\n| `minute` | int | Current match minute |\\n| `league` | str | League/competition name |\\n| `started_at` | datetime | Match start timestamp |\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### `GET /api/matches/{match_id}`\\n\\n**Description:** Get detailed information for a specific match by ID.\\n\\n**Parameters:**\\n\\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\\n|-----------|------|-------------|\\n| `match_id` | int | The unique match identifier (required) |\\n\\n**Response Code:** `200 OK` or `404 Not Found`\\n\\n**Success Response:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"home_team\\\": \\\"FC Sparta Prague\\\",\\n  \\\"away_team\\\": \\\"FC Slavia Prague\\\",\\n  \\\"home_score\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"away_score\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"minute\\\": 67,\\n  \\\"league\\\": \\\"Czech Liga\\\",\\n  \\\"started_at\\\": \\\"2026-03-21T01:30:00\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Error Response (404):**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Match not found\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### `GET /api/matches/{match_id}/stats`\\n\\n**Description:** Get detailed statistics for a specific match.\\n\\n**Parameters:**\\n\\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\\n|-----------|------|-------------|\\n| `match_id` | int | The unique match identifier (required) |\\n\\n**Response Code:** `200 OK` or `404 Not Found`\\n\\n**Success Response:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"possession\\\": {\\n    \\\"home\\\": 55,\\n    \\\"away\\\": 45\\n  },\\n  \\\"shots\\\": {\\n    \\\"home\\\": 12,\\n    \\\"away\\\": 8\\n  },\\n  \\\"shots_on_target\\\": {\\n    \\\"home\\\": 5,\\n    \\\"away\\\": 3\\n  },\\n  \\\"fouls\\\": {\\n    \\\"home\\\": 8,\\n    \\\"away\\\": 11\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Statistics Object Schema:**\\n\\n| Field | Type | Description |\\n|-------|------|-------------|\\n| `possession` | object | Ball possession percentage |\\n| `shots` | object | Total shots taken |\\n| `shots_on_target` | object | Shots on target count |\\n| `fouls` | object | Fouls committed |\\n\\n**Error Response (404):**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Match not found\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### API Documentation\\n\\nInteractive API documentation is available at:\\n\\n- **Swagger UI:** `http://localhost:8000/docs`\\n- **ReDoc:** `http://localhost:8000/redoc`\\n\\n## Running the Server\\n\\n### Development Mode\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npython -m app.main\\n```\\n\\nOr using uvicorn directly:\\n\\n```bash\\nuvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\\n```\\n\\n### Production Mode\\n\\n```bash\\nuvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --workers 4\\n```\\n\\n**Recommended Production Flags:**\\n\\n| Flag | Description |\\n|------|-------------|\\n| `--host 0.0.0.0` | Listen on all network interfaces |\\n| `--port 8000` | HTTP port (change if needed) |\\n| `--workers N` | Number of worker processes (recommended: 2-4) |\\n| `--access-log` | Enable access logging |\\n| `--log-level info` | Set logging level |\\n\\n### Using a Process Manager (Recommended for Production)\\n\\n**Systemd Service Example:**\\n\\nCreate `/etc/systemd/system/football-api.service`:\\n\\n```ini\\n[Unit]\\nDescription=Live Football Dashboard API\\nAfter=network.target\\n\\n[Service]\\nUser=klaus-silhan\\nWorkingDirectory=/home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend\\nExecStart=/home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend/venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --workers 2\\nRestart=always\\n\\n[Install]\\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\\n```\\n\\nEnable and start:\\n\\n```bash\\nsudo systemctl enable football-api\\nsudo systemctl start football-api\\nsudo systemctl status football-api\\n```\\n\\n## Configuration Options\\n\\n### Runtime Configuration\\n\\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\\n| `LIVESPORT_URL` | string | `https://www.livesport.cz` | Base URL for live score scraping |\\n| `CACHE_TTL` | int | `60` | Cache expiration time in seconds |\\n| `UPDATE_INTERVAL` | int | `30` | Background data update interval in seconds |\\n| `DEBUG` | boolean | `false` | Enable debug mode (auto-reload, debug logs) |\\n\\n### Cache Configuration\\n\\nThe API uses an in-memory cache with the following characteristics:\\n\\n- **Storage:** Dictionary-based in-memory storage\\n- **TTL:** Configurable per-entry or default from `CACHE_TTL`\\n- **Auto-expiration:** Expired entries are automatically removed on access\\n- **Operations:** `set()`, `get()`, `delete()`, `clear()`\\n\\n### Background Tasks\\n\\nThe application automatically starts background tasks for:\\n\\n1. **Live data fetching** - Periodically fetches updated match data\\n2. **Session management** - Manages HTTP sessions for scraping\\n\\n## Project Structure\\n\\n```\\nbackend/\\n├── app/\\n│   ├── __init__.py\\n│   ├── main.py              # FastAPI application entry point\\n│   ├── api/\\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\\n│   │   └── schemas.py       # Pydantic response schemas\\n│   ├── cache/\\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\\n│   │   └── cache_manager.py # In-memory cache implementation\\n│   └── scraper/\\n│       ├── __init__.py\\n│       ├── livesport_scraper.py  # Livesport.cz scraper\\n│       └── utils.py         # Scraper utilities\\n├── .env.example             # Environment template\\n├── .env                     # Your environment config (create from .env.example)\\n├── requirements.txt         # Python dependencies\\n└── README.md               # This file\\n```\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n### Backend Dependencies\\n\\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\\n|---------|---------|---------|\\n| `fastapi` | 0.109.0 | Web framework |\\n| `uvicorn[standard]` | 0.27.0 | ASGI server |\\n| `aiohttp` | 3.9.1 | Async HTTP client |\\n| `scrapy` | 2.11.0 | Web scraping framework |\\n| `redis` | 5.0.1 | Cache backend (optional) |\\n| `python-dotenv` | 1.0.0 | Environment variable management |\\n| `pydantic` | 2.5.3 | Data validation and settings |\\n| `schedule` | 1.2.1 | Background task scheduling |\\n\\n## Error Handling\\n\\n### HTTP Status Codes\\n\\n| Code | Description |\\n|------|-------------|\\n| `200` | Success |\\n| `404` | Resource not found |\\n| `500` | Internal server error |\\n\\n### Error Response Format\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Error description message\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Production Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Set `DEBUG=false` in `.env`\\n- [ ] Configure production server (uWSGI, Gunicorn, or multi-worker uvicorn)\\n- [ ] Set up reverse proxy (Nginx, Apache)\\n- [ ] Enable HTTPS/TLS\\n- [ ] Configure firewall rules\\n- [ ] Set up logging and monitoring\\n- [ ] Implement proper error tracking (Sentry, etc.)\\n- [ ] Add authentication/authorization if needed\\n- [ ] Implement rate limiting\\n- [ ] Configure proper CORS headers\\n- [ ] Set up database persistence (replace in-memory storage)\\n- [ ] Implement proper scraper logic for production data\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n### Common Issues\\n\\n**1. Port already in use**\\n\\n```bash\\n# Find process using port 8000\\nlsof -i :8000\\n\\n# Kill the process\\nkill -9 <PID>\\n```\\n\\n**2. Module not found errors**\\n\\n```bash\\n# Ensure virtual environment is activated\\nsource venv/bin/activate\\n\\n# Reinstall dependencies\\npip install -r requirements.txt\\n```\\n\\n**3. Environment variables not loading**\\n\\n```bash\\n# Verify .env file exists in backend directory\\nls -la .env\\n\\n# Ensure python-dotenv is imported in main.py\\n```\\n\\n**4. Scraper not fetching data**\\n\\n- Check `LIVESPORT_URL` is accessible\\n- Review scraper implementation in `app/scraper/livesport_scraper.py`\\n- Check network connectivity and firewall rules\\n\\n## License\\n\\nProprietary - All rights reserved.\\n\\n## Support\\n\\nFor issues and questions, contact the development team.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Generated for Live Football Dashboard Project*\\n\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"vllm\",\n      \"model\": \"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059711738\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\\n\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\nI've created a comprehensive backend README.md file. Here's what I included:\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Created:** `backend/README.md` (9.6KB)\\n\\n### Sections Included:\\n\\n1. **Setup Instructions**\\n   - Virtual environment creation\\n   - Dependency installation (`pip install -r requirements.txt`)\\n   - Environment configuration with `.env` setup\\n\\n2. **All API Endpoints** (documented with examples):\\n   - `GET /` - Health check\\n   - `GET /api/live-matches` - Get all live matches\\n   - `GET /api/matches/{match_id}` - Get specific match\\n   - `GET /api/matches/{match_id}/stats` - Get match statistics\\n\\n3. **Configuration Options**\\n   - Environment variables table (LIVESPORT_URL, CACHE_TTL, UPDATE_INTERVAL, DEBUG)\\n   - Cache configuration details\\n   - Background task explanations\\n\\n4. **How to Run the Server**\\n   - Development mode (with reload)\\n   - Production mode (multi-worker uvicorn)\\n   - Systemd service file example for production deployment\\n\\n5. **Additional Production-Ready Content**\\n   - Project structure overview\\n   - Dependencies list with versions\\n   - Error handling documentation\\n   - Production checklist\\n   - Troubleshooting section\\n\\nThe README is clear, well-structured, and ready for production use. It includes Swagger UI/ReDoc links for interactive API testing.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"vllm\",\n      \"model\": \"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774059759754\n    }\n  ],\n  \"truncated\": true,\n  \"droppedMessages\": false,\n  \"contentTruncated\": true,\n  \"contentRedacted\": false,\n  \"bytes\": 15432\n}"}],"details":{"sessionKey":"agent:ceo:subagent:9026def8-ee54-4326-9c30-9f7869effd32","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: Create a comprehensive backend README.md file in the workspace-ceo/backend directory. The README should include:\n\n1. Setup instructions (venv, pip install, .env configuration)\n2. All API endpoints with descriptions\n3. Configuration options\n4. How to run the server\n\nMake it production-ready and clear."}],"timestamp":1774059682569},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nI need to explore the backend code to understand its structure before creating the README, so I'll list the files in the backend directory.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll create a comprehensive backend README.md file. First, let me explore the backend directory to understand the project structure and API endpoints.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_aa0316cf","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774059682574},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nLet me explore the backend directory structure to understand the project before creating the README.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0a603f69","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend -type f -name \"*.py\" | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774059695195},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6f020192","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/app/main.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9aabdeea","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/app/api/schemas.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f290b8fc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/.env.example"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e59f0420","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/requirements.txt"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774059705126},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nNow let me check the scraper and cache modules to understand the full API structure:\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ca6f673f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/app/scraper/livesport_scraper.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_34343153","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"backend/app/cache/cache_manager.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774059708061},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nNow I have a complete understanding of the backend. Let me create a comprehensive README.md file with all the required sections.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nNow I have a complete understanding of the backend. Let me create a comprehensive README.md file:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fef39dcc","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"backend/README.md","content":"# Live Football Dashboard API\n\nA FastAPI-based backend service that provides real-time football match data with caching and scheduling capabilities.\n\n## Features\n\n- Real-time football match tracking\n- In-memory caching with configurable TTL\n- Background task scheduling for live data updates\n- RESTful API endpoints\n- Environment-based configuration\n\n## Setup Instructions\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3.11+\n- pip package manager\n\n### 1. Create Virtual Environment\n\n```bash\ncd backend\npython -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\\Scripts\\activate\n```\n\n### 2. Install Dependencies\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 3. Configure Environment\n\nCopy the example environment file and configure your settings:\n\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n```\n\nEdit `.env` with your configuration:\n\n```env\n# Livesport scraper base URL\nLIVESPORT_URL=https://www.livesport.cz\n\n# Cache time-to-live in seconds (default: 60)\nCACHE_TTL=60\n\n# Data update interval in seconds (default: 30)\nUPDATE_INTERVAL=30\n\n# Enable debug mode (default: false)\nDEBUG=false\n```\n\n**Environment Variables:**\n\n| Variable | Description | Default | Required |\n|----------|-------------|---------|----------|\n| `LIVESPORT_URL` | Base URL for the livesport scraper | `https://www.livesport.cz` | No |\n| `CACHE_TTL` | Cache time-to-live in seconds | `60` | No |\n| `UPDATE_INTERVAL` | Background update interval in seconds | `30` | No |\n| `DEBUG` | Enable debug mode (`true`/`false`) | `false` | No |\n\n## API Endpoints\n\n### Base URL\n\n```\nhttp://localhost:8000\n```\n\n### Endpoints\n\n#### `GET /`\n\n**Description:** API health check and root endpoint.\n\n**Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": \"Live Football Dashboard API\",\n  \"status\": \"running\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n#### `GET /api/live-matches`\n\n**Description:** Get all live football matches.\n\n**Response Code:** `200 OK`\n\n**Response Schema:** Array of `Match` objects.\n\n**Example Response:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"home_team\": \"FC Sparta Prague\",\n    \"away_team\": \"FC Slavia Prague\",\n    \"home_score\": 1,\n    \"away_score\": 0,\n    \"minute\": 67,\n    \"league\": \"Czech Liga\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-21T01:30:00\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 2,\n    \"home_team\": \"Manchester United\",\n    \"away_team\": \"Liverpool\",\n    \"home_score\": 2,\n    \"away_score\": 2,\n    \"minute\": 89,\n    \"league\": \"Premier League\",\n    \"started_at\": \"2026-03-21T01:15:00\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**Match Object Schema:**\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | int | Unique match identifier |\n| `home_team` | str | Home team name |\n| `away_team` | str | Away team name |\n| `home_score` | int | Home team current score |\n| `away_score` | int | Away team current score |\n| `minute` | int | Current match minute |\n| `league` | str | League/competition name |\n| `started_at` | datetime | Match start timestamp |\n\n---\n\n#### `GET /api/matches/{match_id}`\n\n**Description:** Get detailed information for a specific match by ID.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `match_id` | int | The unique match identifier (required) |\n\n**Response Code:** `200 OK` or `404 Not Found`\n\n**Success Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"home_team\": \"FC Sparta Prague\",\n  \"away_team\": \"FC Slavia Prague\",\n  \"home_score\": 1,\n  \"away_score\": 0,\n  \"minute\": 67,\n  \"league\": \"Czech Liga\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-21T01:30:00\"\n}\n```\n\n**Error Response (404):**\n```json\n{\n  \"detail\": \"Match not found\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n#### `GET /api/matches/{match_id}/stats`\n\n**Description:** Get detailed statistics for a specific match.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `match_id` | int | The unique match identifier (required) |\n\n**Response Code:** `200 OK` or `404 Not Found`\n\n**Success Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"possession\": {\n    \"home\": 55,\n    \"away\": 45\n  },\n  \"shots\": {\n    \"home\": 12,\n    \"away\": 8\n  },\n  \"shots_on_target\": {\n    \"home\": 5,\n    \"away\": 3\n  },\n  \"fouls\": {\n    \"home\": 8,\n    \"away\": 11\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Statistics Object Schema:**\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `possession` | object | Ball possession percentage |\n| `shots` | object | Total shots taken |\n| `shots_on_target` | object | Shots on target count |\n| `fouls` | object | Fouls committed |\n\n**Error Response (404):**\n```json\n{\n  \"detail\": \"Match not found\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### API Documentation\n\nInteractive API documentation is available at:\n\n- **Swagger UI:** `http://localhost:8000/docs`\n- **ReDoc:** `http://localhost:8000/redoc`\n\n## Running the Server\n\n### Development Mode\n\n```bash\ncd backend\npython -m app.main\n```\n\nOr using uvicorn directly:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\n```\n\n### Production Mode\n\n```bash\nuvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --workers 4\n```\n\n**Recommended Production Flags:**\n\n| Flag | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `--host 0.0.0.0` | Listen on all network interfaces |\n| `--port 8000` | HTTP port (change if needed) |\n| `--workers N` | Number of worker processes (recommended: 2-4) |\n| `--access-log` | Enable access logging |\n| `--log-level info` | Set logging level |\n\n### Using a Process Manager (Recommended for Production)\n\n**Systemd Service Example:**\n\nCreate `/etc/systemd/system/football-api.service`:\n\n```ini\n[Unit]\nDescription=Live Football Dashboard API\nAfter=network.target\n\n[Service]\nUser=klaus-silhan\nWorkingDirectory=/home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend\nExecStart=/home/klaus-silhan/.openclaw/workspace-ceo/backend/venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --workers 2\nRestart=always\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\n```\n\nEnable and start:\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl enable football-api\nsudo systemctl start football-api\nsudo systemctl status football-api\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\n### Runtime Configuration\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `LIVESPORT_URL` | string | `https://www.livesport.cz` | Base URL for live score scraping |\n| `CACHE_TTL` | int | `60` | Cache expiration time in seconds |\n| `UPDATE_INTERVAL` | int | `30` | Background data update interval in seconds |\n| `DEBUG` | boolean | `false` | Enable debug mode (auto-reload, debug logs) |\n\n### Cache Configuration\n\nThe API uses an in-memory cache with the following characteristics:\n\n- **Storage:** Dictionary-based in-memory storage\n- **TTL:** Configurable per-entry or default from `CACHE_TTL`\n- **Auto-expiration:** Expired entries are automatically removed on access\n- **Operations:** `set()`, `get()`, `delete()`, `clear()`\n\n### Background Tasks\n\nThe application automatically starts background tasks for:\n\n1. **Live data fetching** - Periodically fetches updated match data\n2. **Session management** - Manages HTTP sessions for scraping\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nbackend/\n├── app/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── main.py              # FastAPI application entry point\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   └── schemas.py       # Pydantic response schemas\n│   ├── cache/\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   └── cache_manager.py # In-memory cache implementation\n│   └── scraper/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── livesport_scraper.py  # Livesport.cz scraper\n│       └── utils.py         # Scraper utilities\n├── .env.example             # Environment template\n├── .env                     # Your environment config (create from .env.example)\n├── requirements.txt         # Python dependencies\n└── README.md               # This file\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Backend Dependencies\n\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `fastapi` | 0.109.0 | Web framework |\n| `uvicorn[standard]` | 0.27.0 | ASGI server |\n| `aiohttp` | 3.9.1 | Async HTTP client |\n| `scrapy` | 2.11.0 | Web scraping framework |\n| `redis` | 5.0.1 | Cache backend (optional) |\n| `python-dotenv` | 1.0.0 | Environment variable management |\n| `pydantic` | 2.5.3 | Data validation and settings |\n| `schedule` | 1.2.1 | Background task scheduling |\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### HTTP Status Codes\n\n| Code | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `200` | Success |\n| `404` | Resource not found |\n| `500` | Internal server error |\n\n### Error Response Format\n\n```json\n{\n  \"detail\": \"Error description message\"\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] Set `DEBUG=false` in `.env`\n- [ ] Configure production server (uWSGI, Gunicorn, or multi-worker uvicorn)\n- [ ] Set up reverse proxy (Nginx, Apache)\n- [ ] Enable HTTPS/TLS\n- [ ] Configure firewall rules\n- [ ] Set up logging and monitoring\n- [ ] Implement proper error tracking (Sentry, etc.)\n- [ ] Add authentication/authorization if needed\n- [ ] Implement rate limiting\n- [ ] Configure proper CORS headers\n- [ ] Set up database persistence (replace in-memory storage)\n- [ ] Implement proper scraper logic for production data\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n**1. Port already in use**\n\n```bash\n# Find process using port 8000\nlsof -i :8000\n\n# Kill the process\nkill -9 <PID>\n```\n\n**2. Module not found errors**\n\n```bash\n# Ensure virtual environment is activated\nsource venv/bin/activate\n\n# Reinstall dependencies\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n**3. Environment variables not loading**\n\n```bash\n# Verify .env file exists in backend directory\nls -la .env\n\n# Ensure python-dotenv is imported in main.py\n```\n\n**4. Scraper not fetching data**\n\n- Check `LIVESPORT_URL` is accessible\n- Review scraper implementation in `app/scraper/livesport_scraper.py`\n- Check network connectivity and firewall rules\n\n## License\n\nProprietary - All rights reserved.\n\n## Support\n\nFor issues and questions, contact the development team.\n\n---\n\n*Generated for Live Football Dashboard Project*\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"1e20fd8d42056f870933bf98ca6211024744f7ec","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774059711738},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've created a comprehensive backend README.md file. Here's what I included:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Created:** `backend/README.md` (9.6KB)\n\n### Sections Included:\n\n1. **Setup Instructions**\n   - Virtual environment creation\n   - Dependency installation (`pip install -r requirements.txt`)\n   - Environment configuration with `.env` setup\n\n2. **All API Endpoints** (documented with examples):\n   - `GET /` - Health check\n   - `GET /api/live-matches` - Get all live matches\n   - `GET /api/matches/{match_id}` - Get specific match\n   - `GET /api/matches/{match_id}/stats` - Get match statistics\n\n3. **Configuration Options**\n   - Environment variables table (LIVESPORT_URL, CACHE_TTL, UPDATE_INTERVAL, DEBUG)\n   - Cache configuration details\n   - Background task explanations\n\n4. **How to Run the Server**\n   - Development mode (with reload)\n   - Production mode (multi-worker uvicorn)\n   - Systemd service file example for production deployment\n\n5. **Additional Production-Ready Content**\n   - Project structure overview\n   - Dependencies list